Well, I just ascended, and I have to admit I found completing the Quest 
and the other branches more much more enjoyable than going through
Hell itself, which seemed more an endurance test.

So I suggest an alternate way of completing the game. As about everyone
knows, there is a wand of wishing in Fort Knox, and the first thing
you should wish for is a blessed scroll of recharging. Rather than 
wasting days (literally) going through Hell, why not then return to level 1,
wish for the Amulet of Yendor, and ascend to the elemental planes for the
end game battle, avoiding the part of the dungeon that exists simply to
keep you and the amulet appart?

Advantages:
	* No "Cheap plastic copy of the Amulet of Yendor" mistakes.
	* No ascending staircase problems (You sometimes skip back down
          a level or two once you have the amulet).  
	* None of the "twisty little maze where all the passages look alike"
	  monotonousness that lower Hell falls into.
	* No Wizard of Yendor beating you up every fifth level on the way up
	  trying to get the amulet: You're only carrying a wand of wishing.
	* Complete the game in 20-60 hours less time.

Disadvantages:
	* Miss the amulet of life saving and boots of water walking
	  in Vlad's tower. Miss the fun of Medusa's island, although
	  there's no artifacts there.
	* I didn't see any wraiths until I was in Hell myself. Need to
	  eat those wraiths and get up to level 30 if you're
	  to survive the elemental planes. 
	* Finding the magic portal to Fort Knox, like finding any magic portal,
	  is a pain. (Is there an artifact that can map magic portals?) 
	* I believe the Fort Knox level only exists *sometimes* in your dungeon.
	  But you can rub lamps, sit on thrones after you have your luck maxed
	  out etc. until you can wish for a wand of wishing and follow
          this same shortcut.

Comments? 


